138 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 108 0 R
/E (Accurately recovering an "attack story" and identifying key malicious system entities is vital but difficult, often requiring redundant manual efforts and high-level domain expertise. Frequent false alarms caused by "concept drift" \(natural changes in system behavior over time\) often tire and confuse security analysts, potentially leading to missed detections. Enterprises generate hundreds of GB of audit logs daily, creating massive computation and memory overhead.  )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
